======================================================================================================================
6. MUTATION CONTROLS
======================================================================================================================
  [PASS] M103a a null perturbation must return exactly the unperturbed a_0 -- otherwise the machinery leaks   (max |log10 ratio| over 5 null draws = 0.00e+00)
  [PASS] M103b inflating a channel's input error by 3x must inflate its contribution by 3x (the propagation is linear over this range), so the budget is a real propagation and not a fitted number   (Upsilon zero-point at 3x: 0.0451 dex vs 3 x 0.0121 = 0.0362)
  [PASS] M103c halving the sample must shrink the RANDOM total by sqrt(2) and leave the COHERENT total alone -- the test that the random/coherent split is real and not a labelling choice   (random 0.0308 -> 0.0452 (ratio 1.47, expected 1.41); coherent 0.0665 -> 0.0619 (ratio 0.93, expected 1.00))

======================================================================================================================
VERDICT -- ITEM 103
======================================================================================================================
  The deep-tail a_0 estimator's error budget, decomposed, on the corrected (full-kernel) estimator:

                             distance  inclination    Upsilon      gas    V_obs    TOTAL
    all deep tail              0.0444       0.0189     0.0531   0.0110   0.0103   0.0733   dex
    f_gas > 0.7                0.0591       0.0264     0.0443   0.0154   0.0192   0.0822   dex
    f_*,loc < 0.2              0.0585       0.0301     0.0128   0.0280   0.0154   0.0742   dex

  1. THE TWO BLOCKERS ARE DISTANCE AND THE UPSILON ZERO-POINT, and which one leads depends on the cut.  On the
     full deep tail they are comparable (0.053 dex Upsilon against 0.044 distance); on the gas-dominated cuts
     distance takes over completely.  a_0 ~ D^-2.2 (not D^-2: the kernel is not asymptotic in the tail), and
     SPARC's median distance error is 14%, so distance never falls below 0.044 dex on any cut.  The hunt's
     standing conclusion that 'the blocker is the stellar mass-to-light ratio' holds for the LENSING items and the
     per-galaxy fits; for THIS estimator, removing Upsilon leaves an error that is barely smaller, because the
     distance term grows as the sample shrinks.  That is why item 102's M/L-free measurement is 15% and not 8%.
  2. THE FLOOR WITH UPSILON REMOVED is 10.5% -- the distance SCALE (8.8%) and the HI mass
     scale (5.5%) added in quadrature.  Neither shrinks with sample size.
  3. THE CUT THAT REACHES 3% DOES NOT EXIST.  'f_*,loc < 0.2 with a TRGB or Cepheid distance' is the right cut and
     it needs ~124 galaxies where SPARC has 8 -- a factor 16 in sample size; and even at infinite N
     the distance zero-point holds it at
     10.5%.  3% in a_0 requires the distance ladder to 1.3%, which nobody has.
  4. AGAINST INTEREST: with the coherent terms in, no deep-tail measurement separates the two footings, and item
     64's kappa becomes 0.482 +- 0.081 rather than 0.512 +- 0.076 -- still consistent with 1/2, still excluding
     1/(2 pi), but at lower significance and from a lower central value.

